    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0594" n="582" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24546/39: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Wellington</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cox</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wellington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-25T11:00:00+12:00">November 25,
                            1941—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 25—6:57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s November 22, 4 p.m. Prime Minister states that the New Zealand
                    Government understands and agrees to this matter.</p>
                <p>He has asked me to express his gratification for the message contained in your
                    November 13, 11 p.m.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d576-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cox</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
